ed_by":null},{"id":8133949121,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAAB5NI2wQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:i18n","name":"topic:i18n","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":5,"created_at":"2025-01-12T21:48:29Z","updated_at":"2025-10-27T15:11:48Z","closed_at":"2025-10-27T15:11:13Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101471","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101471","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101471.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101471.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"Fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101464\r\n\r\nReuses same plural rule string format and handling code as PO/MO translations.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure what's the best way to handle it in CSV, I have simply done parsing of multiple plural forms as subsequent lines with the same key and special `_PluralRule` line, e.g, CSV with plural forms can look like:\r\n\r\n| keys | fr |  _Comment  |\r\n| --- | --- | --- |\r\n| _PluralRule | \"nplurals=2; plural=(n >= 2);\"   | Rule string |\r\n| \"There are %d apples\" | \"Il y a %d pomme\" | Singular form      |\r\n| \"There are %d apples\" | \"Il y a %d pommes\" | First plural form  |\r\n\r\nNote: `get_plural_message` function has `plural_text` argument, which is not used by PO/MO translation, I have not used it either, and not sure why it was added, but have not removed it to avoid breaking compatibility since it is passed to GDScript/GDExtension `Translation` implementations.\r\n\r\n- *Production edit: This closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/1291\r\n and closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/41519 by superseding it.*","closed_by